.TH SEED-SD 8 2026-10-19 "Peios prelude 0.0.7"
.SH NAME
seed-sd \- seed security descriptors on a filesystem tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seed-sd
.RB [ \-r | \-\-recursive ]
.RB [ \-\-sddl " " \fIdescriptor\fR ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seed-sd
sets the owner, group, and discretionary access control list on a path.
It initializes access control on newly mounted filesystems and device nodes.
It stamps a symlink itself rather than following its target.
.PP
The default descriptor names SYSTEM as owner and group. Its DACL grants
GenericAll to SYSTEM and Administrators, inheritable by objects and
containers. A third entry grants GenericAll to CREATOR OWNER with object
inheritance, container inheritance, and inherit-only set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r , " " \-\-recursive
Seed the path and each existing descendant. Each node is seeded before it is
read, allowing traversal into a previously unmanaged directory. Symlinks are
not descended into. A failed operation is reported and the walk continues
where possible; changes already made are not rolled back.
.TP
.BI \-\-sddl " descriptor"
Use this SDDL descriptor instead of the bootstrap default. The last supplied
descriptor wins. Invalid input fails without falling back to the default.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing. Use this before a path beginning with a dash.
.PP
Exactly one path is required. Unknown options, a missing descriptor argument,
extra paths, and arguments containing invalid UTF-8 are usage errors.
Paths must be representable as UTF-8;
recursive traversal reports unrepresentable descendant paths as failures.
.SH SECURITY
Replacing a missing descriptor requires SeRestorePrivilege. Updating an
existing descriptor requires the applicable WRITE_DAC and WRITE_OWNER
access. The kernel enforces these checks.
.PP
The bootstrap default grants nothing to Everyone. Broadening this default
for /dev would also broaden access to inherited raw disk nodes. Supply a
separate descriptor only when the target tree's policy requires it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every requested operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Descriptor construction or at least one filesystem operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B seed-sd -r /dev
Seed existing device nodes and establish the default inherited descriptor
for nodes created afterward.
.PP
.B seed-sd -- -data
Seed a path whose name begins with a dash.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prelude (8)
